.TH fmt_urlencoded 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/textcode"
.SH NAME
fmt_urlencoded \- Convert a string to URL-encoded format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/textcode.h>
.sp
.BI "size_t fmt_urlencoded(char* dest, const char* src, size_t len)"
.sp
.BI "size_t fmt_urlencoded2(char* dest, const char* src, size_t len, const char* escapeme)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function .BR fmt_urlencoded () converts a string to URL-encoded format. The function takes the following parameters:
.sp
1. A pointer to the destination buffer.
2. The source string.
3. The length of the source string.
.sp
The function returns the number of bytes written to the destination buffer.
.SH SYNOPSIS
The function .BR fmt_urlencoded2 () converts a string to URL-encoded format with additional escaping. The function takes the following parameters:
.sp
1. A pointer to the destination buffer.
2. The source string.
3. The length of the source string.
4. A string containing characters to be additionally escaped.
.sp
The function returns the number of bytes written to the destination buffer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes written to the destination buffer, or (size_t)-1 on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for this function.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B issafe, stralloc_readyplus
